{"sectionId":"circulation/blood","items":[{"id":"circulation--blood-k001","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"혈액은 혈장과 세포 성분으로 구성되며 albumin은 교질삼투압 유지에 중요하다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k002","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"성숙 인간 적혈구는 핵과 미토콘드리아가 없으며 해당과정으로 ATP를 얻는다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k003","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"hemoglobin은 heme의 Fe²⁺에 산소를 가역 결합하며 협동성으로 S자형 결합곡선을 나타낸다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k004","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"pH 감소, CO₂ 증가, 온도 상승, 2,3-BPG 증가 등은 일반적으로 산소 친화도를 낮춘다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k005","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"EPO는 저산소 반응에 따라 적혈구 생성을 촉진한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k006","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"혈관 손상 시 vWF와 혈소판 GPIb가 부착에 관여하고 활성화된 GPIIb/IIIa와 fibrinogen은 응집을 매개한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k007","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"응고 연쇄는 factor X 활성화로 수렴해 thrombin을 만들고 fibrinogen을 fibrin으로 전환한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k008","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"vitamin K는 II,VII,IX,X 및 protein C,S의 γ-carboxylation에 필요하다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k009","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"tPA에 의해 plasminogen이 plasmin으로 활성화되면 fibrin 분해가 촉진된다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k010","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"ABO 혈액형은 적혈구 항원과 혈장 항체를 구별해 수혈 적합성을 판단한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k011","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"Bohr 효과: H⁺/CO₂ 증가에 따른 Hb 산소 친화도 감소.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k012","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"헤모글로빈과 미오글로빈 결합곡선은 다르다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k013","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"혈청은 응고 후 얻은 액체, 혈장은 항응고 혈액의 액체 성분이다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k014","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"혈소판 부착과 응집 수용체를 구별한다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"circulation--blood-k015","sectionId":"circulation/blood","unitId":"circulation","subject":"biology","text":"우측으로 이동한다.","kind":"review-answer","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]}]}